3. I have to deploy an application. In which scenario you will choose EC2 & Lambda?
When deciding between deploying an application on EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) versus AWS Lambda, I would consider the following scenarios:
1. Use EC2 when: 
   - The application requires full control over the operating system and environment.
   - The application needs to run for extended periods or has long-running processes.
   - The application requires specific software or configurations not available in Lambda.
   - The application has high memory or CPU requirements that exceed Lambda's limits.
2. Use Lambda when:
   - The application is event-driven and can be broken into small, independent functions.
   - The application has variable traffic and needs to scale automatically.
   - The application is serverless and doesn't require managing servers or infrastructure.

